# FILLET Experiment 2a with HEXTOR 4.2.1-42-g75f5fb1
# Model: HEXTOR 4.2.1-42-g75f5fb1 (FILLET re-file, September 2026); 18 latitude belts of 10 deg, seasonal cycle, explicit 730 steps per orbit (dt = 43226.5 s, set by nstepyr).
# Radiation: 1 bar lookup table ./radiation/radiation_N2_CO2_Sun.h5 (clear sky; CO2 axis 100 ppm - 0.91, T 190-370 K with power-law extrapolation outside; CO2 below 100 ppm is clamped to the axis floor); no cloud albedo (fcloud = 0); cloudir = 0.00 W m^-2 (untuned).
# Transport: D = 0.50 W m^-2 K^-1 constant (diffadj off); the Diff column is the value used.
# Surface: surface albedo ocean 0.20 / land 0.30 / snow-ice 0.60; heat capacities land 1e7, water 4e8, ice 1e7 J m^-2 K^-1; ocean fraction 0.75 in every belt; sea-ice fraction 1 - exp((T - 273.15 K)/10 K) between 273.15 and 263.15 K and 1 below; land snow below 273.15 K.
# Orbit: a varied with S = S_earth / a^2, e = 0, year = 365.22 d x a^1.5.
# Initial state: uniform 288 K (warm start) or 233 K (cold start) as noted per experiment; every case starts from that state (no continuation).
# Convergence: halt when the year-to-year change in global-mean OLR falls below 1e-03 W m^-2, or when it repeats to that tolerance over a cycle of up to 4 years (a periodic seasonal oscillation; the case then reports one phase of the cycle) (cap 5000 orbits); one further orbit provides the annual means. Per-case records in logs/.
# Numerics switches: diffcons = .true..
#
# Name of benchmark/experiment: Experiment 2a
# Initial state for this experiment: uniform 233 K (cold start)
# Describe how ice line latitude is determined: latitude where the annual-mean belt temperature crosses 263.15 K, linearly interpolated between belt centres. Ice-free: NMin = 90, SMax = -90; snowball: NMin = 0, SMax = 0. A cap coexisting with a belt in one hemisphere is reported as the cap (noted in logs/).
#
# Columns of data
# Case = case number (0 -> total number of cases in experiment)
# Inst = instellation (S_earth; i.e., relative to Earth's 1361 W m^-2)
# Obl = obliquity (degrees)
# XCO2 = mixing ratio (volume) of CO2 (ppm)
# Tglob = global, annual mean surface temperature (K)
# IceLineNMax = latitude of northern edge of ice in northern hemisphere (deg)
# IceLineNMin = latitude of southern edge of ice in northern hemisphere (deg)
# IceLineSMax = latitude of northern edge of ice in southern hemisphere (deg)
# IceLineSMin = latitude of southern edge of ice in southern hemisphere (deg)
# Diff = diffusion coefficient actually used by the run (W m^-2 K^-1)
# OLR = global, annual mean outgoing longwave radiation (W m^-2)
#
# Examples for IceLine max and min:
# Polar caps: IceLineNMax = 90, IceLineNMin = 60, IceLineSMax = -60, IceLineSMin = -90
# Snowball state: IceLineNMax = 90, IceLineNMin = 0, IceLineSMax = 0, IceLineSMin = -90
# Ice free state: IceLineNMax = 90, IceLineNMin = 90, IceLineSMax = -90, IceLineSMin = -90
# Ice belt: IceLineNMax = 30, IceLineNMin = 0, IceLineSMax = 0, IceLineSMin = -30
# Note ice belt doesn't really have "edges" at 0 deg, but record as 0 anyway to
# keep the columns the same length
#
# Case Inst Obl XCO2 Tglob IceLineNMax IceLineNMin IceLineSMax IceLineSMin Diff OLRglob
